<facsimile><graphic url="https://www.e-manuscripta.ch/i3f/v20/1079129/manifest"/></facsimile><text><body><div type="letter">
<pb facs="1079130" n="1"/>
  <opener><salute>Viro <choice><abbr>Illustriss.</abbr><expan>Illustrissimo</expan></choice> et <choice><abbr>Celeber.<hi rend="sup">o</hi></abbr><expan>Celeberrimo</expan></choice>
      <lb/><rs key="pers_DE-588-118509969" type="person">Joanni Bernoulli</rs>
      <lb/><rs key="pers_DE-588-102552517" type="person">Petrus Antonius Michelotti</rs> <abbr>S. P. D.</abbr></salute></opener>
  <p><lb/>Accessit ad me hodie amicus quidam meus
      <lb/>excusation<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> ferens cujusdam Patritii qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ograv">ò</g></orig><reg>o</reg></choice>d
      <lb/>amiserit <rs type="lostletter">epistolam</rs><note type="editorial" resp="SG">Francesco Fabris hatte das für Michelotti bestimmte Schreiben Johann I Bernoullis einem venezianischen Patrizier übergeben, der es laut Michelotti verlor. Das Schreiben enthielt wohl die Frage, ob <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-118656503">Daniel I Bernoulli</rs> seine medizinische Ausbildung in Venedig fortsetzen könne. Darauf weisen Michelottis <rs type="letter" key="B_991170515151005501">Brief</rs> vom 6. April und Bernoullis <rs type="letter" key="B_991170515150905501">Brief</rs> vom 11. April 1720.</note> quandam tuam ad me
      <lb/>pertinentem sibique a <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-1343364833">Fabris</rs> traditam.
      <lb/>Ab hoc eodem amico intelligo <choice><abbr>Excell.<hi rend="sup">um</hi></abbr><expan>Excellentissimum</expan></choice> Virum
      <lb/>Comitem Joannem <rs key="pers_DE-588-121710742" type="person">Vezzi</rs> <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-1343364833">Fabris</rs> usum
      <lb/>fuisse ut <choice><abbr>Doctiss.</abbr><expan>Doctissimum</expan></choice> Fili<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> Tuum <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Nicolaum</rs>
      <lb/>tanqu<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> Mathemat<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> Magistr<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> huc in
      <lb/>dom<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> su<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> conduceret. <del>Veloti</del> <add>Uti</add> gaudeo quod
      <lb/><choice><abbr>Ornatiss.</abbr><expan>Ornatissimus</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filius</rs> Tuus redeat <rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetias</rs>, ita
      <lb/>doleo qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ograv">ò</g></orig><reg>o</reg></choice>d ego non habuerim honorem trac<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>tandi hanc rem, de qua pridem scripseram
      <lb/>ad <choice><abbr>Celeber.rimum</abbr><expan>Celeberrimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnat<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>, ad quem ultimo scrip<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>si null<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> esse spem conducendi huc ips<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>
      <lb/><choice><abbr>Doctiss.<hi rend="sup"/></abbr><expan>Doctissimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filium</rs> Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>. Patritius hic nunquam
      <lb/>mecum de hac re locutus est, sed ante tres
      <lb/>aut quatuor menses misit ad me amic<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> sci<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>scitantem de <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filio</rs> Tuo, de ejus moribus, de
      <lb/>ejus ingenio, deque ejus habilitate in rebus
      <lb/>mathematicis. Eodem tempore amicus hic sci<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>scitabatur num <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filius</rs> Tuus oblato honorifico
<pb facs="1079131" n="2"/>
      <lb/>stipendio veniret <rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetias</rs>. Laudavi primum
      <lb/>et quidem justissime <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Fili<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> Tuum, tum respondi
      <lb/>me nescire an rediturus esset <rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetias</rs> quoni<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>
      <lb/><rs key="place_GEO-2925177" type="place">Friburgi</rs> degere <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">e<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> intellexi: quod tamen scrip<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>siss<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice>. Scripsi ad <choice><abbr>Illustriss</abbr><expan>Illustrissimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnat<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> Tuum de hac
      <lb/>re. Qui respondit perlibenter scire velle quis
      <lb/>esset Patritius de quo loquebamur, qu<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice>nam essent
      <lb/>conditiones etc. Mense Januarii adivi amic<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> ut
      <lb/>informationem acciper<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> de salario, de conditio<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>nibus offerendis <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filio</rs> Tuo. Amicus respondit
      <lb/>Patriti<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> uti Filium Famili<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice> mutasse
      <lb/>opinionem, et non audere vocare amplius
      <lb/><rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Fili<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> plures excusationes addens neque
      <lb/>mihi dicens eti<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> rogatus quis esset Patritius
      <lb/>ipse. En ration<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> ob qu<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> ita scripsi postremo
      <lb/>ad <choice><abbr>Illustriss.</abbr><expan>Illustrissimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnat<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs> Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>. Hodie ergo Amicus et ego
      <lb/>demiramur rem secreto et clam tractatam fuisse
      <lb/>a <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-1343364833">Fabris</rs>, ad quem, <del>neque</del> <add>aut</add> ad quenquam alium
      <lb/>degentem <rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetiis</rs> rogo ut deinceps meas
      <lb/>litteras <add>non</add> mittas. Cupio enim ut easdem
      <lb/>ad me mittas. Te rogo ut mihi significes
      <lb/>quid contineretur in tua <rs type="lostletter">epistola</rs> quam ad
      <lb/>me scribebas. Nollem enim ut eam perlegissent
<pb facs="1079132" n="3"/>
      <lb/>pr<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice>sertim si aliquid spectans ad meam <rs key="biblio_M3G2JA79" type="biblio">Disserta<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>tionem</rs> in ea continebatur. Ceterum uti hodie
      <lb/>scivi quis esset Patritius ita te certior<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> facio eum
      <lb/>esse Filium Patris valde divitis. Erat enim ante
      <lb/>tres annos circiter, Mercator Adamant<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice>, et
      <lb/>factus fuit Patritius. Generose ergo tractabitur
      <lb/>et nobilissime ab hoc Patritio, cujus mores sunt
      <lb/>humanissimi, et optimi. Mihi gaudeo, vobisque
      <lb/>gratulor de hac re. De mea Dissertatione<note type="editorial" resp="SG">Michelotti hatte <rs type="person" key="pers_DE-588-119166895">Nicolaus I Bernoulli</rs> im <rs type="letter" key="B_991170517025805501">Brief</rs> vom 2. März 1720 gebeten, das Manuskript über Mailand zurückzuschicken. Im <rs type="letter" key="B_991170517025705501">Brief</rs> vom 10. März schlug er auch Bergamo als Rückweg vor.</note>,
      <lb/>si eam perlegisti, rogavi <choice><abbr>Illustriss.</abbr><expan>Illustrissimum</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnatum</rs>
      <lb/>Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> ut quam prim<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> eand<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> ad me mitteret
      <lb/>tela ceracea obvolut<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> atque obsignat<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice>. Rogo
      <lb/>iter<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> de hac re promittendo solvere omnes
      <lb/>expensas quas facietis remittendo eam ipsam
      <lb/>Dissertation<choice><orig><g ref="#em">ē</g></orig><reg>em</reg></choice> a Te benigne correctam nedum
      <lb/>attente perlectam. Tuo permissu Teque dante
      <lb/>aut jubente, efficiam ut una cum mea Disserta<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>tione in public<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice> prodeant Tu<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice> doctissim<choice><orig><g ref="#ae">æ</g></orig><reg>ae</reg></choice>
      <lb/>Dissertationes <rs key="biblio_JAFFCHKU" type="biblio">de Motu Musculor<choice><orig><g ref="#um">ū</g></orig><reg>um</reg></choice></rs>, et <rs key="biblio_W6BHQDM2" type="biblio">de Effer<pc type="hyphenation">-</pc><lb break="no"/>vescentia, et Fermentatione</rs><note type="editorial" resp="SG">Michelotti gab Bernoullis beide Dissertationen 1721 in Venedig bei den Brüdern Pinelli in einer gemeinsamen Neuausgabe unter dem Titel <rs type="biblio" key="biblio_LUTG2JUY">Dissertationes physico-mechanicae</rs> heraus und fügte seine <hi rend="i">Animadversiones X</hi> zu Keill bei. Michelottis eigene Dissertation <hi rend="i">De separatione fluidorum in corpore animali</hi> erschien mit eigenem Titelblatt und eigener Seitenzählung. Im <rs type="letter" key="B_991170515150205501">Brief</rs> vom 2. Mai 1721 berichtet Michelotti, er habe beide Drucke in einem Paket über Mailand an Bernoulli geschickt.</note>.</p> <closer><salute>Vale, me amare
      <lb/>perge, et salutem plurimam dicito <choice><abbr>Cl.</abbr><expan>Clarissimo</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-117589144" type="person">Filio</rs> Tuo
      <lb/>(quem hic expecto) et <choice><abbr>Ill.</abbr><expan>Illustrissimo</expan></choice> <rs key="pers_DE-588-119166895" type="person">Agnato</rs>.</salute>
<dateline>Dab<choice><orig><g ref="#am">ā</g></orig><reg>am</reg></choice> <rs key="place_GEO-3164603" type="place">Venetiis</rs>
      <lb/><choice><abbr>a.</abbr><expan>ante</expan></choice> <choice><abbr>d.</abbr><expan>diem</expan></choice> <date when="1720-03-22">22 Martii 1720.</date></dateline></closer>
<pb facs="1079133" n="4" type="empty"/>
</div></body></text></TEI>